config ONTHE15_KEYMAP_FORCE_STOCK
    bool "Discard any stored keymap at boot and run the compiled one"
    depends on ZMK_KEYMAP_SETTINGS_STORAGE
    default n
    help
      Hardware-test images want the deterministic compiled keymap (the shield's
      A-Z-in-physical-order layout), but ZMK_STUDIO_RPC hard-selects
      ZMK_KEYMAP_SETTINGS_STORAGE, so a board that already carries a saved
      keymap would boot into that instead. Enable this to call
      zmk_keymap_reset_settings() shortly after startup, which deletes the
      stored bindings, layer names and layer ordering and reloads the stock
      keymap - the same thing ZMK Studio's "restore stock keymap" does.

      Only the keymap is touched: lighting, battery, BLE bonds and every other
      settings subtree are left alone, unlike a full settings erase.

      Never enable this in a distributed or daily-use image: keymap edits made
      over Studio will not survive a reboot.
